     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>In this model, angfrus and calm are parallel mediators.</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">one_ind &lt;- &#39;disob_f ~ home_f + angfrus + calm # c and b paths<br>            angfrus ~ home_f<br>            calm ~ home_f # a path<br>            calm~~angfrus&#39;<br><br></font></div><div>They are two different paths:<br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\"><br></font></div><div>home_f -&gt; angfrus -&gt; disob_f<br></div><div>home_f -&gt; calm -&gt; disob_f<br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\"><br></font></div><div>This will work:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">out_fit1_angfrus &lt;- indirect_effect(x = &quot;home_f&quot;,<br>                                    m = c(&quot;angfrus&quot;),<br>                                    y = &quot;disob_f&quot;,<br>                                    fit = fit1,<br>                                    boot_ci = TRUE,<br>                                    R = 10,</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">                                    seed = 2345)<br>out_fit1_clam &lt;- indirect_effect(x = &quot;home_f&quot;,<br>                                 m = c(&quot;calm&quot;),<br>                                 y = &quot;disob_f&quot;,<br>                                 fit = fit1,<br>                                 boot_ci = TRUE,<br>                                 R = 10,</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">                                 seed = 2345)</font><br></div><div><br></div><div>Make sure that you set the seed, to ensure that the same B bootstrap samples are used across analyses, or use do_boot() to generate bootstrap estimates that can be reused across analyses. (But see the next paragraph on bootstrapping with clustering ...)</div><div><br></div><div>By the way, I noticed that you used cluster. I am not sure how lavaan handles bootstrapping when &#39;cluster&#39; is used. Bootstrapping conducted in manymome tries to mimic what lavaan does, to ensure the results are consistent with those of lavaan. If done internally, manymome uses casewise resampling, which ignores clustering. I am not sure how lavaan does bootstrapping when the argument &#39;cluster&#39; is used. (I would like to know more about this but will ask in another post.)</div><div><br></div><div>If you would like to form CIs for the indirect effects while using MLR with clustering in sem(), you can use the Monte Carlo confidence intervals. It uses the variance-covariance matrix generated by lavaan to form the Monte Carlo CI intervals, and so you can use whatever estimation method you like when calling sem(). E.g.,</div><div><font face=\"Courier New\"><br></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">out_fit1_angfrus &lt;- indirect_effect(x = &quot;home_f&quot;,</span><br style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">                                    m = c(&quot;angfrus&quot;),</span><br style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">                                    y = &quot;disob_f&quot;,</span><br style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">                                    fit = fit1,</span><br style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">                                    mc_ci = TRUE,</span><br style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">                                    R = 10,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">                                    seed = 4567)</span><br></div><br>Again, the two mediators are in parallel and you need two calls to indirect_effect(). You should set the seed to the same number, or pregenerage the MC simulated estimates using do_mc() and reuse the output (<a href=\"https://sfcheung.github.io/manymome/articles/do_mc.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sfcheung.github.io/manymome/articles/do_mc.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414335051000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0G027MXSzYIwyyVf8bu_Iw\">https://sfcheung.github.io/manymome/articles/do_mc.html</a>).<div><br><div>Hope this helps.<div><br></div><div>-- Shu Fai</div><div><br></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, September 5, 2024 at 10:55:54 PM UTC+8 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ajsu...@appliedanalyses.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">When I run this code<div><br></div><div>one_ind&lt;-&#39;disob_f~home_f+angfrus+calm # c and b paths<br>angfrus~home_f <br>calm~home_f# a path<br>calm~~angfrus&#39;<br>fit1&lt;-sem(one_ind,data=df,cluster=&quot;T_ID&quot;,estimator=&quot;mlr&quot;)<br>summary(fit1)<br><br>out_fit1&lt;-indirect_effect(x=&quot;home_f&quot;,m=c(&quot;angfrus&quot;,&quot;calm&quot;),y=&quot;disob_f&quot;,<br>              fit=fit1,<br>              boot_ci=T,<br>              R=10)</div><div><br></div><div>I get this error that I don&#39;t understand</div><div><br></div><div><pre aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in cond_indirect(x = x, y = y, m = m, fit = fit, est = est, implied_stats = implied_stats,  : \r\n  No path from ‘home_f’ to ‘disob_f’ through ‘angfrus’, ‘calm’. Please check the arguments x, y, and m.</span></span></pre><pre aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><br></span></span></pre><pre aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Any help is appreciated, Andy</span></span></pre><div><br></div><span class=\"gmail_signature_prefix\">-- </span><br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><a href=\"http://www.appliedanalyses.com\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.appliedanalyses.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414335052000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EsR1HuhLAXEXxb70Il2Sn\">www.appliedanalyses.com</a></div><div><i><a href=\"http://goog_596703989\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://goog_596703989&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414335052000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ou-j5Fe9WIJFkFJ2xy8Hi\"><br></a></i></div><div><i>PayPal QR Code</i></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><i><br></i></div><div><br><br><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/mail-sig/AIorK4xKd7Zr-R6F9y0lPU4jsV0y9dQLVqirSdZ1RVJd8apIRG-W0BfSh_kbvkZDTeZGmZTGvJTtTXOGiUgc\"><br><br></div><div><p><i><a href=\"http://goog_596703989\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl